      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Vulvodynia is a difficult management problem. In this review article, the clinical subsets of vulvodynia including recurrent vulvovaginal candidiasis, vulvar vestibulitis syndrome and dysaesthetic vulvodynia are described. Their aetiology is discussed and available therapies are presented."},
